        <div id="who-should-buy" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            10. Is Naked Mass Healthy, and Who Should Buy It?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Naked Mass is a clean product by label standards, but whether it is healthy depends on whether you need the calories. One serving of the unflavored version has 252 g of carbohydrate, more than many adults eat in a whole day, and most of it is fast-digesting maltodextrin. For someone underweight or training hard and unable to eat enough, that is the point. For anyone else, it is simply a lot of extra energy.
          </p>

          <p>
            Several groups should talk to a doctor or registered dietitian first. That includes anyone with diabetes or prediabetes, because of the carbohydrate load; anyone with kidney disease, because of the protein; people who are pregnant, especially for the vegan version with its lead warning; and anyone who has lost weight without trying, which needs a diagnosis rather than a gainer. Older adults with medical conditions should check too.
          </p>

          <p>
            Naked says Naked Mass is suitable for teenagers because of its short ingredient list. A teenager who is genuinely struggling to gain weight may benefit, but most active teens can get the same calories from food, and a growing athlete is better served by a plan from a pediatrician or sports dietitian. Our <a href="/best-protein-powder-for-teens/">protein powder for teens guide</a> covers the gentler options.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Who should buy Naked Mass</h3>

          <p>
            Buy the unflavored whey version if you are a hard gainer who wants the fewest ingredients and no sweeteners and will blend it with real food. Buy Vegan Naked Mass if you are lactose intolerant or vegan and need the same calories. Buy the chocolate version if you will only drink a gainer that tastes sweet, and accept 58 g of sugars as the trade-off.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Who should skip it</h3>

          <p>
            Skip it if you want protein without many extra calories; Naked Whey or Naked Pea is almost certainly what you meant to buy. Skip it if you are a drug-tested athlete who needs NSF Certified for Sport, and skip it if the lowest cost per serving is the deciding factor, since Dymatize Super Mass Gainer or a homemade shake is cheaper. For dairy-free protein without gainer calories, see our <a href="/best-lactose-free-protein-powder/">lactose-free protein powder guide</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

